                                          | name             |
                                          | availability     |
                                          +------------------+

Multiplicities:
Patient 1.. Appointment*
Practitioner 1.. Appointment*
Appointment links both

Design Rationale:
The domain model focuses on three core entities, patient, practitioner and appointments.
These represent the essential real world concepts described in the Smartcare case study.
Responsibilities were allocated based on what each entitiy naturally owns, patients for 
example storing personal details, practitioners store availability, and appointments store
scheduling information. Relationships reflect real clinic operations like patients and 
practioners both have many appointments, while each appointment links exactly one patient
and one practinoner. Optional classes such as clinic were excluded from the core model 
because they reprsent syste level aggregation rather than domain concepts. Tehnical constructs
like manager, controllers, or databases were intertionally excluded because they belong to software
architecture, not the domain model.

AI Design Review Record:
| AI Suggestion          | Evidence          | Decision     | Reason                                      | Model Change |
|------------------------|-------------------|--------------|---------------------------------------------|--------------|
| PatientManager         | None              | Rejected     | Implementation detail, not domain concept   | None         |
| PractitionerManager    | None              | Rejected     | Same as above                               | None         |
| AppointmentManager     | None              | Rejected     | Not a domain entity                         | None         |
| ClinicController       | None              | Rejected     | Controller belongs to UI/logic layer        | None         |
| NotificationManager    | Out of scope      | Rejected     | SmartCare v0.2 has no notifications         | None         |
| ScheduleEngine         | None              | Rejected     | Over-engineered for small clinic            | None         |





